  "review_decisions": [
    "Use the corpus Fourier convention with 2 pi in the exponential.",
    "Define all real Sobolev orders together and retain the low-frequency integrability condition.",
    "Whole-space smooth density is asserted only for finite p; cutoff estimates require only local gradient integrability.",
    "Select the plus-i Riesz convention; its double product has the negative quadratic symbol required by the pressure equation.",
    "Construct pressure for L1 tensors by a bounded Fourier function, without extending a nonsmooth multiplier to arbitrary tempered distributions.",
